WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.401 --> 00:00:15.962
Anyone passing a certain smiling young lady skipping down the street would have assumed that she was happy.

2
00:00:15.963 --> 00:00:20.402
In fact, Jo was more than happy; she was ecstatic.

3
00:00:20.403 --> 00:00:29.222
She was sure to be spotted and gossiped about as she sprinted like a wild horse on a public street, but at this moment in time, she did not care.

4
00:00:29.223 --> 00:00:34.227
She felt like a free pony, released from captivity into the wild.

5
00:00:34.228 --> 00:00:39.836
Her captor: Grumpy, difficult Aunt March. Her release: Summer holidays.

6
00:00:39.837 --> 00:00:45.833
Every summer Aunt March took a trip to Europe, often staying until the beginning of autumn.

7
00:00:45.834 --> 00:00:52.901
Although Jo secretly prayed that Aunt March would ask her to accompany her one day (as Jo had always longed to see Europe),

8
00:00:52.902 --> 00:00:56.405
still it was pure joy not to have to work all summer.

9
00:00:56.406 --> 00:01:01.770
Jo pitied those poor souls who were trapped indoors on this glorious sunny afternoon.

10
00:01:01.771 --> 00:01:04.983
One of them, she noted when she got to her house,

11
00:01:04.984 --> 00:01:13.329
was probably sitting at the table with his books opened but his thoughts wandering off as he impatiently waited for his lessons to end.

12
00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:20.044
Turning toward Laurie's library, where the window was wide open, Jo called out in a teasing voice,

13
00:01:20.045 --> 00:01:28.374
"I wonder what I will do tomorrow since I can do whatever I want, unlike some people who must study their lessons."

14
00:01:28.375 --> 00:01:34.253
Just as Jo had predicted, Laurie popped his head out the window and called out playfully,

15
00:01:34.254 --> 00:01:41.658
"Excuse me, would you mind keeping your voice down? Some of us are trying to get better educated, thank you very much."

16
00:01:41.659 --> 00:01:46.553
Laughing loudly, Jo wiggled her foot at him, their signature greeting now.

17
00:01:46.554 --> 00:01:52.780
Waving his foot back, Laurie called down, "Are you off now? Have your holidays begun?"

18
00:01:52.781 --> 00:01:59.192
"Yes!" shouted Jo. "And I am ever so happy. I have so many things I want to do!"

19
00:01:59.193 --> 00:02:02.385
"Well, I hope I am included in some of your plans.

20
00:02:02.386 --> 00:02:11.506
I have absolutely nothing to do this summer, so I'm counting on you girls to keep me entertained and out of trouble," Laurie said with a wink.

21
00:02:11.507 --> 00:02:16.373
"Don't worry, friend, we'll have ourselves a ball," Jo promised.

22
00:02:16.374 --> 00:02:21.042
Waving at Laurie, Jo hopped and skipped up to her house and went in,

23
00:02:21.043 --> 00:02:27.982
but not before she heard Mr. Brookes reprimanding Laurie for interrupting their discussion on the French Revolution.

24
00:02:27.983 --> 00:02:31.448
By coincidence Meg also got an early summer holiday

25
00:02:31.449 --> 00:02:38.195
because the Kings had unexpectedly decided to visit their relatives in California and were planning to leave shortly.

26
00:02:38.196 --> 00:02:44.180
Needless to say the girls were thrilled at the prospect of spending the summer without the burden of work.

27
00:02:44.181 --> 00:02:47.371
"Then may Beth and I get an early holiday as well?"

28
00:02:47.372 --> 00:02:51.169
Amy had asked as soon as she heard her sisters' good news.

29
00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:56.668
After much discussion with Mother, Meg and Jo decided the girls could have a few extra weeks

30
00:02:56.669 --> 00:03:01.239
to bask in the sun as long as they still did some homework every now and then.

31
00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:09.368
Content with that arrangement, Amy promptly shut her book and began working on her new art project, namely oil painting.

32
00:03:09.369 --> 00:03:16.708
On the eve of their first day of summer vacation, the girls made many plans about what they were going to do with all that time.

33
00:03:16.709 --> 00:03:19.614
"I want to go fishing," Jo started.

34
00:03:19.615 --> 00:03:27.389
"I don't want to do anything at all; just go outside and paint, draw, and sleep," Amy said dreamily.

35
00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:30.889
Mother, carrying in a stack of clothes to be mended, remarked,

36
00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:37.910
"We have plenty to do around the house and since Father isn't here, we need to make repairs before the winter and…"

37
00:03:37.911 --> 00:03:42.183
Mother stopped talking when she noticed the girls had long faces.

38
00:03:42.184 --> 00:03:45.398
"Whatever is the matter, girls?" she asked.

39
00:03:45.399 --> 00:03:50.702
Meg looked at Jo, who looked at Amy, who looked at Beth, who looked back at Meg.

40
00:03:50.703 --> 00:03:55.754
Mother waited patiently, watching this wordless communication with amusement.

41
00:03:55.755 --> 00:04:02.639
"Well, we thought, since it is our holiday, that—" Meg looked pleadingly at Jo.

42
00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:06.455
"That we'd like a holiday," Jo finished for Meg,

43
00:04:06.456 --> 00:04:13.954
"Not just from work and school, but also from our chores and not to have to worry about repairs; just to be lazy."

44
00:04:13.955 --> 00:04:18.841
"Do you think it would be relaxing if you did nothing at all?" Mother asked.

45
00:04:18.842 --> 00:04:25.773
"We are going to do things," Amy stated, "just things that we want to do; not what we have to do."

46
00:04:25.774 --> 00:04:28.732
The others nodded their heads in agreement.

47
00:04:28.733 --> 00:04:36.180
"I understand," Mother said, "but I must warn you that being lazy and relaxing are not the same thing.

48
00:04:36.181 --> 00:04:41.879
But this may be a good learning experience for you girls. Let's try an experiment."

49
00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:47.138
Jo jumped up and cried passionately, "I love experiments!"

50
00:04:47.139 --> 00:04:54.606
"Starting tomorrow, for one week," said Mother, "you girls can do whatever you want, whenever you want to do it.

51
00:04:54.607 --> 00:05:01.266
Hannah and I will continue to do our share of the housework and cook, but you will not have to do yours."

52
00:05:01.267 --> 00:05:05.887
Here, Mother was interrupted by loud shouts of joy and clapping.

53
00:05:05.888 --> 00:05:12.497
She held up her hand to silence them and then continued, "But you must keep this up for one full week."

54
00:05:12.498 --> 00:05:15.621
"That won't be too hard," giggled Amy.

55
00:05:15.622 --> 00:05:22.706
"Don't be too sure, Amy," warned Mother. "Doing nothing is harder than you think. Now, what do you say?"

56
00:05:22.707 --> 00:05:28.416
"Let the lazy summer experiment begin!" shouted Jo.

57
00:05:28.417 --> 00:05:33.348
The first day of the experiment was just as wonderful as the girls imagined.

58
00:05:33.349 --> 00:05:39.426
They slept until they wanted, got up whenever they felt like it, and did whatever they liked.

59
00:05:39.427 --> 00:05:44.794
Beth, on an empty stomach, ran over to Mr. Laurence's house to play the grand piano.

60
00:05:44.795 --> 00:05:48.765
Meg chose the arduous task of sitting in the sun and doing nothing.

61
00:05:48.766 --> 00:05:54.526
Amy decided to paint Meg doing nothing and took all her oil paints outside to set up her easel.

62
00:05:54.527 --> 00:06:04.342
Jo, with one of her favorite books on hand, joined her sisters nearby, and soon the March girls, minus one, were enjoying their lazy summer morning.

63
00:06:04.343 --> 00:06:11.633
"Ah, isn't this relaxing?" sighed Meg, turning her face up toward the warm rays of the sun.

64
00:06:11.634 --> 00:06:16.446
"Hold still, Meg," cried Amy as she tried to capture her sister's face.

65
00:06:16.447 --> 00:06:22.288
"Will you please be quiet so I can read in peace?" Jo called out from under a shady tree.

66
00:06:22.289 --> 00:06:30.540
As the sisters soaked up the sun in serenity, they could hear the faint sounds of Beth playing the grand piano at Mr. Laurence's mansion.

67
00:06:30.541 --> 00:06:37.792
Of course, even lazy people get hungry, so when Jo could no longer ignore the growling of her stomach she said,

68
00:06:37.793 --> 00:06:42.097
"I'd better eat something or my stomach will complain."

69
00:06:42.098 --> 00:06:45.553
"Yes, I'm getting hungry, too," said Meg.

70
00:06:45.554 --> 00:06:51.889
"I'll come as well," Amy said, abandoning her paintbrush and colors without a second glance.

71
00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:59.870
The three sisters went inside to the kitchen expecting some food to be ready for them but they were startled to see nothing on the table.

72
00:06:59.871 --> 00:07:07.045
Laughing, Meg confessed, "I think it was my turn to make lunch and I forgot completely. I'm sorry."

73
00:07:07.046 --> 00:07:14.543
"No need to apologize, my dear," Jo said graciously, "we're on holiday. I'm sure we can find something to eat."

74
00:07:14.544 --> 00:07:20.612
Searching high and low, the girls finally found some stale bread and butter, which they washed down with cold tea.

75
00:07:20.613 --> 00:07:26.423
"Let's go back to relaxing then," said Jo, patting her still growling stomach.

76
00:07:26.424 --> 00:07:31.165
The girls did just that.
